Zoe (docs): Quick sync  heads-up we need a tiny troubleshooting example for the error-ref: how to handle 429s that return partial content. Current guidance is too vague. Can someone sketch a compact SDK-friendly snippet and a 1-line migration note?

Alec (sdk): I can draft JS+Py micro-snippets. Proposal: message-level trimming (dont drop system messages), honor Retry-After if >=1s, otherwise bounded exponential backoff with jitter. Keep each example under ~12 lines.

Ravi (eng-runtime): +1. Runtime now sets `x-partial-ok: 1` on partial responses and surfaces `err.partialResponse` in the SDK. Recommend logging it so apps can reconcile before replaying side-effects. Also `Retry-After` can be fractional; treat <1s as noise.

Sofia (devex): Well need two short UI strings for the docs callout: "Trying trimmed context" and "Retrying after backoff". I can add ES/FR locales after copy lands.

Alec (sdk): Draft JS snippet (compact):

```js
// drop oldest non-system messages, honor Retry-After, retry with backoff
async function sendSafe(client, convo, opts={}){
  for(let attempt=0; attempt<3; attempt++){
    try{return await client.generate({conversation:convo});}
    catch(e){
      if(e.status!==429) throw e;
      const ra=parseFloat(e.headers?.['retry-after']||'0');
      await sleep(ra>=1?ra*1000:Math.pow(2,attempt)*300 + Math.random()*100);
      while(convo.length && tokenCount(convo) > (opts.targetTokens||2600)){
        if(convo[0].role==='system') break; convo.shift();
      }
    }
  }
  throw new Error('retries exhausted');
}
```

Alec (sdk): Python variant added to PR description; both snippets link to sdk retry util: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/blob/main/src/retry-utils.ts

Ravi (eng-runtime): Please add a one-line operator callout: "If your app applies side-effects on model output, check `err.partialResponse` or `x-partial-ok` before retrying to avoid duplicate side-effects."

Zoe (docs): Will add a bold callout: "Do not trim system/instruction messages." Also include a 1-line migration tip: "Switch ad-hoc handlers to sdk.retryUtils.trimAndRetry to get consistent behavior across SDKs."

